{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 39, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "**A Whirlwind Adventure in Japan**\n\nLast month, I spent two weeks in Japan, a country that effortlessly blends tradition and innovation. My journey began in **Tokyo**, where gleaming skyscrapers stood beside historic temples. The hum of neon lights in **Shibuya** gave way to serene moments in **Asakusa’s**Sensorji Temple, its incense-scented alleys whispering centuries of history. A stop at **Tsukiji Outer Market** rewarded me with sushi so fresh it still shimmered with ocean mist, devoured alongside miso soup under a paper umbrella.\n\nFrom the city’s chaos, I fled to the **Japanese Alps**. **Hakone’s** hot springs cradled me in silk-robed relaxation, while **Lake Ashi** reflected Mount Fuji’s elusive silhouette. A cable car ride rewarded me with views so breathtaking I forgot to breathe.\n\n**Kyoto** was a masterclass in elegance—cherry blossoms in **Maruyama Park**, kimono-clad geisha glimpsed through bamboo groves, and matcha whisked into foam at a teahouse. The **Fushimi Inari** shrine’s torii gates stretched endlessly, a labyrinth of crimson prayers.\n\nMy final stop was **Osaka**, where street food stalls served takoyaki and okonomiyaki until my waistline protested. The **Osaka Castle** grounds offered a quiet farewell, its stone walls heavy with samurai tales.\n\nJapan is a symphony of contrasts: the high-tech efficiency of bullet trains, the ritual of tea ceremony, the quiet poetry of a single cherry blossom. It’s a country that doesn’t just welcome you—it enchants you, leaving you with a longing to return.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.06550939381122589}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.27843376994132996}, {"token": " Wh", "logprob": -0.037113383412361145}, {"token": "irl", "logprob": -0.018043426796793938}, {"token": "wind", "logprob": -4.7801782784517854e-05}, {"token": " Adventure", "logprob": -0.8805687427520752}